From 000424254bdeee45c1dd692325aee83f8db70237 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anurodh Pokharel <anurodhp@icloud.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 20:56:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] common/aaplbfct.cpp: guard NSSystemDirectories.h include
 by TARGET_OS_EMBEDDED

Real header gap on any iOS/embedded SDK (confirmed: Xcode 12's
iPhoneOS.sdk has no NSSystemDirectories.h -- it's a macOS-only Libc
private header), but the include was already dead weight there: its
only real use (NSSearchPathEnumeration/NSLibraryDirectory/etc, inside
loadDictionaryMatcherFor) is already wrapped in the file's own
'#if !TARGET_OS_EMBEDDED' / '#if 0' guard a few lines below -- just the
#include itself was left unconditional. TargetConditionals.h is already
guaranteed included transitively before this point (via unicode/utypes.h
-> platform.h, per this file's own comment on its later explicit
re-include), so TARGET_OS_EMBEDDED is available here. Confirmed via a
standalone preprocess that TARGET_OS_EMBEDDED=1 for
arm64-apple-ios14.4, i.e. this project's actual cross-compile target
already takes the embedded, NSSystemDirectories-free path Apple's own
guard says it should.
---
 icuSources/common/aaplbfct.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/icuSources/common/aaplbfct.cpp b/icuSources/common/aaplbfct.cpp
index 7dbafa700..f80c6e645 100644
--- a/icuSources/common/aaplbfct.cpp
+++ b/icuSources/common/aaplbfct.cpp
@@ -21,7 +21,9 @@
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <glob.h>
 #include <strings.h>
+#if !TARGET_OS_EMBEDDED
 #include <NSSystemDirectories.h>
+#endif
 #include <sys/types.h>
 #include <sys/stat.h>
 #include <sys/mman.h>
-- 
